From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0351-lichii-gpu-0213-uniform-banks-uploaded-directly.patch

Source: 0351-lichii-gpu-0213-uniform-banks-uploaded-directly.patch
buffer_cache: upload native 64 KiB uniform banks directly (EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT=1)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 176 (mja00), dbcbe547b3, GPL-3.0-or-later.

Patch 0039 re-uploads these banks once a frame by marking them CPU-modified. That unprotects and
reprotects their pages and moves the write epoch 0017 checks, so ranges nearby get walked again.
With the switch the bank is copied there and then. The PR's author saw 18% on his machine; that
number does not carry over.

Runs on the PS5: yes, for any 64 KiB bank of a Switch 2 program. Not known how many Ocarina binds.
Behaviour: the same bytes reach the buffer, one step earlier in the draw.
Hang: adds no new kind of wait. The upload is the one SynchronizeBuffer does, and it can wait for
the stream ring as that does (0095). Pool memory: none.
Checked: PS5-target syntax compile of the buffer cache. Not run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 7b54a2dfa6..885b806670 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -1440,8 +1440,23 @@ void BufferCache<P>::BindHostGraphicsUniformBuffer(size_t stage, u32 index, u32
                device_memory.template GetPointer<u8>(device_addr + mapped_size) != nullptr) {
             mapped_size += Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE - ((device_addr + mapped_size) & Core::DEVICE_PAGEMASK);
         }
-        if (mapped_size != 0) {
-            memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsCpuModified(device_addr, (std::min<u64>)(mapped_size, size));
+        // From Lichii PR 176 (zortos293/Lichii, dbcbe547b3). EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT=1 copies the
+        // bank here: marking it CPU-modified unprotected and reprotected its pages each frame, and
+        // moved the write epoch SynchronizeBuffer checks, so ranges nearby were walked again.
+        static const bool bank_direct = [] {
+            const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UBO_BANK_DIRECT");
+            return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+        }();
+        const u64 upload_size = (std::min<u64>)(mapped_size, size);
+        if (upload_size != 0 && bank_direct) {
+            std::array<BufferCopy, 1> copies{BufferCopy{
+                .src_offset = 0,
+                .dst_offset = buffer.Offset(device_addr),
+                .size = upload_size,
+            }};
+            UploadMemory(buffer, upload_size, upload_size, copies);
+        } else if (upload_size != 0) {
+            memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsCpuModified(device_addr, upload_size);
         }
     }
     const bool use_fast_buffer = needs_alignment_stream
